            <listPerson>
                <person xml:id="PAT03" sex="1">
                    <persName>Colonel <roleName/>
                        <forename>Daniel </forename>
                        <surname>Paterson</surname>
                        <addName/>
                    </persName>
                    <birth when="1738">
                        <placeName/>
                    </birth>
                    <death when="1824"/>
                    <occupation>Soldier</occupation>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p>See Ed Pope's note: Colonel Paterson (27.2.1798) was probably Daniel
                            Paterson DNB 1738-1825, although he only became Lt Col on 1.1.1798 and
                            although Johnson never published his books of Roads, he was the only
                            Colonel Paterson or Patterson in army lists for 1798, including militia
                            and Indian army lists. Col Patterson of Dean St Soho subscr 1800 to
                            Wildman was probably him. Whether the Patersons after 1802 were him I
                            rather doubt but I can't otherwise identify them at present. </p><p>We
                            have coded this as a single contact - but, clearly, we cannot be certain
                            entries subsequent to his appearance are Samuel Paterson (until 1802) or
                            Daniel.</p>
                    </note>
